{
	title: 'Model picker sets effort',
	spec: `The shared terminal/web model picker selects a model AND its supported thinking effort from task w7. The tree from zg remains intact. On category rows, Right expands and Left collapses (or moves to the parent when already closed), exactly the category navigation contract; on model leaves, Right raises effort one supported step and Left lowers it one step, clamped at the endpoints, never wrapping. Model leaves are not collapsible, so leaf Left no longer jumps to the parent: this is the deliberate resolution of the zg conflict. Up/Down still navigate rows; Esc cancels the entire draft. Ctrl-A/E still move in the search text; Left/Right retain these row-context actions while filtering. Do not capture emergency keys.

Effort uses the ordered filtered capability list, never numeric positions shared between different providers. Opening highlights the current bare model and initializes its leaf to the sessions actual effective effort. Other leaves start at their capability defaults. Visiting another leaf remembers its draft for this modal only; neither arrows nor category expansion change the live session. On the first adjustment from an omitted default, choose the neighboring supported level around the effective known default; if the effective default is unknown, Right chooses the lowest supported level and Left the highest, and show that distinction. An unsupported model has a clear no-effort-control label and arrows do nothing on its leaf, not accidentally select a provider. Enter on a leaf commits its draft through the same host-validated model:level resolver as /model. Enter on a category with a default chooses that default model at its default effort, except when it is the current model, where the existing session effort is preserved. Category defaults without a model still only expand. Canceling or reconnecting never persists an unconfirmed draft; selecting another client concurrently is host-validated with the same rules.

Every leaf visibly shows its selected effort or the providers default/unknown label alongside display name/id without destroying fuzzy match ranges. Header shows current model+effort; help text explains category Left/Right versus leaf lower/higher and endpoint behavior. Search matches the base model/category words rather than manufacturing duplicate leaves for each effort. Switching models does not carry an unsupported effort. The picker receives browser-safe capability descriptions in its existing host modal payload; clients do not discover capabilities over HTTP or duplicate provider heuristics. On the web, equivalent Lower/Higher controls on the selected model leaf are keyboard-operable and have accessible names including the selected level, disabled endpoints and >=44px touch targets. They adjust only the modal draft; clicking the model itself or confirming commits model+effort. Preserve zgs phone visual-viewport sizing, wrapped full model names and no horizontal clipping; live effort changes must not rebuild the whole list or lose scroll/focus.

Tests exercise the actual shared picker state transitions: categories keep expansion, leaves change only supported levels, endpoints clamp, colon-bearing ids remain unchanged, filtering keeps tree state, Enter submits the correct pair and Esc submits nothing. A small terminal/web manual check covers help, narrow/phone wrapping, accessible controls and focus. No snapshots of model catalogs or provider API matrices duplicated here. Scope is picker interaction/presentation only; effort persistence, provider mapping, status row and direct syntax belong to w7.`,
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Precedents: Claude Code model picker Left/Right effort (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/model-config); Pi Shift+Tab cycle (https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/blob/1b347794e2a630e4359f2584f4eea388145d0ddf/packages/coding-agent/docs/keybindings.md); OpenCode variants via Ctrl+T, per-model variant dictionaries (https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/f66b86ceec1a497417f750b88a06cf6923c5c75f/packages/tui/src/config/keybind.ts and packages/opencode/src/provider/transform.ts). Hal uses contextual arrows instead of adopting those global shortcuts. zg category expansion stays; only leaf Left changes from parent navigation to lowering effort. This task deliberately follows w7 to avoid separate UI/API level lists.',
		'One-time headless Chrome check at 390x844 (touch emulation) and 1280x844: current Opus default medium, Higher changes modal draft to high, all row DOM nodes retained, Higher button retains focus and accessible name updates, 44px controls, no horizontal overflow, category/leaf help visible, cancel leaves session effort unchanged. The check caught and fixed the old effect stealing button focus back to Search on draft updates. Kept shared state-transition tests, removed temporary browser check to avoid ongoing test debt.',
		'Terminal one-time frame check at 45 and 90 columns: effort now precedes model names/ids on leaf rows so narrow clipping cannot hide the selected level; selected-leaf lower/higher (clamped) help is first. Tree arrows, draft-only changes and Escape cancellation were exercised through the shared picker and terminal client handlers. Header and full names remain subject to the existing terminal single-line clipping contract.'
	],
	needs: ['w7', 'zg', '0x', 'dz']
